NOTICE: this program runs popsicle circuit PSI from Swanky, which its README calls research software,
not for production or sensitive data. The two parties are threads of this one process,
joined by an in-process socket pair. Data: synthetic keys made by this program; nothing is read
from or written to disk, and results print to this terminal only. Limits: one case per run; the process ends after 10 s and keeps one CPU core busy until then.
It deliberately drives upstream into sessions that do not complete.
Unresolved: results are samples from one host and one target (x86_64); behaviour elsewhere is untested, and no result here establishes a security property of Swanky.
It reproduces upstream behaviour at a pinned commit and establishes no security property.
It creates no persistent state.
